1,GPIO,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,Register Read/Write Validation,"This test validates the default reset values and read-write accessibility of GPIO registers gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, and gp0_gpio_10. It first reads each register after reset and compares the value against expected defaults. Then it writes six distinct test patterns to each writable register, reads back the values, and verifies correctness using read and write masks. The test reports pass if all default value checks and all write-read-back checks succeed for every register, and fail otherwise.","1. Initialize the test environment and load register address, default value, read mask, and write mask arrays for the GPIO registers under test.
2. Perform default reset value check: For each of the three GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10), read the register value, apply a bit mask, and compare against the expected default reset value. Skip registers flagged in the reset-skip array or those that are not readable.
3. Record any default value mismatches and increment the default failure counter.
4. Perform write-read-back validation: For each of six predefined test data patterns, write the pattern (masked by the write mask) to each writable GPIO register.
5. Read back each register after writing, apply the read mask, and compute the expected value considering both the write mask and default values for non-writable bits.
6. Compare the read-back value against the expected value. Record any mismatches and increment the write failure counter.
7. Repeat steps 4-6 for all six test patterns across all three GPIO registers.
8. Determine final test verdict: PASS if no default value mismatches and no write-read mismatches occurred; FAIL otherwise.","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","All three GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10) must return expected default reset values after reset. All six write-read-back test patterns must produce matching read-back values when accounting for read masks, write masks, and default values of non-writable bits. Both failure counters must remain zero for the test to pass.",NA,NA,"The test uses six distinct data patterns to exercise all bit positions. Read and write masks are applied to account for read-only, write-only, and read-write fields. Bit 0 is masked out during default value checking. Registers flagged in skip arrays are excluded from respective checks. The soft reset check function is disabled (dead code).",GPIO,gp0_gpio_8,0xA001A000,0x0,32,data_in,0,RO,0x0,read_modify_write,"Determines the level gpio pin. Read returns the current value of the corresponding pin regardless of whether the pin is an input or an output"
