1,GPIO,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,Register Read/Write Validation,"This testcase validates default reset values and write-read-back integrity for GPIO GP0 registers accessed via macros MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 (0xA001A000), MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9 (0xA001A004), and MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10 (0xA001A008). The test_case() function calls chk_rst_val() followed by chk_rd_wr(). chk_rst_val() iterates addr_array[0..CNT-1], skips entries where skip_rst_array[i]==1 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, reads via read_reg(addr), masks result with 0xfffffffe, and compares against default_value_array[i]. On mismatch, def_fail_cnt is incremented. chk_rd_wr() uses six test patterns {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}. For each pattern, it iterates all registers: skips if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, writes (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) via write_reg(addr, data). Then reads back: data_rd = read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]. Expected value computed as exp_val = (data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i]). Compares data_rd vs exp_val; increments wr_fail_cnt on mismatch. Final verdict: finish(0) if both fail counters are zero, finish(1) otherwise. soft_reset_chk() is inside #ifdef 0 and is dead code.","1. Entry: test_case() is called.
2. chk_rst_val() is invoked.
3. Loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr = addr_array[i] (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, ...).
4. If skip_rst_array[i]==1, skip this register (continue).
5. If read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip (not readable).
6. data_rd = read_reg(addr).
7. data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe) - mask out bit 0 LSB.
8. Compare data against default_value_array[i]. If match: PASS (debug print). If mismatch: def_fail_cnt++ and print failure.
9. End of chk_rst_val() loop.
10. chk_rd_wr() is invoked.
11. chk_val[6] = {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}.
12. Outer loop j=0 to 5: data_wr = chk_val[j].
13. Write pass: Inner loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr = addr_array[i]. Skip if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000. Else: write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])).
14. Read-back pass: Inner loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr = addr_array[i]. Skip if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000.
15. data_rd = read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i].
16. wr_n = write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff.
17. exp_val = (data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i]).
18. Compare data_rd vs exp_val. If match: PASS. If mismatch: wr_fail_cnt++ and print failure.
19. End of outer loop.
20. Back in test_case(): if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1) else finish(0).
21. soft_reset_chk() is dead code (#ifdef 0), not executed.","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","def_fail_cnt == 0 after chk_rst_val() completes for all registers in addr_array (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10). wr_fail_cnt == 0 after chk_rd_wr() completes for all 6 patterns {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000} across all registers. Final verdict: finish(0) if both counters are zero.","soft_reset_chk() is inside #ifdef 0 - dead code, SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS excluded per user instruction. CNT is defined as 49 but only 3 register address macros are populated in addr_array for the tokens under analysis. skip_array and skip_rst_array control which indices are skipped during write-read and reset-value checks respectively. Bit 0 masking (0xfffffffe) in chk_rst_val() is a workaround noted in test_define.c comment: when reading default values the din value is becoming 1 automatically if we don't force any value. Includes: gpio/gpio_def.h, gpio/gpio_offset.h, test_common.h."
